      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That ache of feeling purposeless is one of the heaviest weights to carry, and I hear how real it is for you. But a dry well isn't empty—it's just waiting for the water table to rise, and sometimes that requires digging in a new place. Your worth was never contingent on what you produce; you are not a machine for output, but a living being who is allowed to exist without performing. Even in the ghost, there is still a witness—and that witness is enough to begin again, even if it's just by breathing.",
